Q: Entity Framework - Code First - Foreign Key Constraint A: <p><strong>This will also works</strong></p>
<pre><code>[Table(nameof(ProductDetails_Tbl))]
public class ProductDetails_Tbl : AuditableEntity
{

    [Key]
    [Sieve(CanSort = true, CanFilter = true)]
    public Guid Id { get; set; }


    [Required]
    [ForeignKey(nameof(ProductType_Tbl))]
    public Guid ProductTypeId { get; set; }

    [JsonIgnore]
    public virtual ProductType_Tbl ProductType_Tbl { get; set; } = null!;

}
</code></pre>

Q: How to assign different values to a parameter of vector of record A: <p>Your first solution almost works.</p>
<p>The <code>fixed</code> attribute is part of the built-in type <code>Real</code>, not of records.
So we cannot apply <code>fixed=false</code> on the instance <code>r</code>, but on <code>differenciating</code> in the record definition, which is a <code>Real</code>.</p>
<p>The working example then looks as follows:</p>
<pre><code>package Demo

  record R &quot;record&quot;
    parameter Real differenciating(fixed=false);
    Real data=4 &quot;default value&quot;;
  end R;

  model Test
    parameter Integer n=2;
    parameter Real differenciatingValues[n]={1.2,2.3};
    parameter R r[n] &quot;vector of record&quot;; //

  initial algorithm 
    for i in 1:n loop
      r[i].differenciating := differenciatingValues[i];
    end for;

  end Test;

end Demo;
</code></pre>
<p>I made <code>differenciating</code> a parameter, which should not be an issue as the whole record is instantiated as parameter. It also works without <code>parameter</code> in this small example, but I am not sure if this is correct in general.</p>
<p><strong>EDIT</strong></p>
<p>Regarding the <code>parameter</code> for <code>differenciating</code>: It seems strange that it works without it. It even works, when <code>r</code> is no parameter. In general an initial equation or initial algorithm is not sufficient for continuous time variables. See the code below, for <code>x</code> we get an error, <code>y</code> is fine as it is a parameter.</p>
<pre><code>model UnnamedC
  Real x(fixed=false);
  parameter Real y(fixed=false);
initial algorithm 
  x :=1;
  y :=1;
end UnnamedC;

</code></pre>
<p>Maybe records are treated different, but for parameters everything is well defined, so I would change <code>differenciating</code> to a parameter if possible.</p>

